                            <comment id="506744" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:33:08 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Single occurrence: sanity-sec test_55 'Autotest time out' on review-ldiskfs-ubuntu (Ubuntu 22.04 client, change 57999 ps1, 2025-02-07). The same signature has not recurred in Rainshadow in the 21 months since. The test's later failures (umount /mnt/lustre failed, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18461" title="Lustre join file re-implementation" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18461"&gt;LU-18461&lt;/a&gt; join work; mgs/trusted_nodemap mismatch; remount failed) are different signatures. The listed leads (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14121" title="EACESS Permission denied for slurm log files when using nodemap with admin=0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14121"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14121&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; nodemap squashing, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14327" title="Interop: sanity-sec test 55 fails with “test_55 failed with 13”" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14327"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14327&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; skip for old servers, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18171" title="Update sanity-sec test cases for IPv6" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18171"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18171&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; IPv6) do not match a hang. Change 57999 only touches pcc.c, which test_55 does not exercise. I did not try to reproduce on a VM, since the hang was Autotest-side with no log pointing at test_55 itself. Leaving open; if it recurs, attach the client/MDS stack dumps.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
